# Railway Backend Deployment Guide

## Step 1: Push to GitHub
1. Create a GitHub repo
2. Push this project to GitHub:
   git init
   git add .
   git commit -m "Initial commit"
   git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/blackbox.git
   git push -u origin main

## Step 2: Deploy Backend on Railway
1. Go to https://railway.app
2. Sign up with GitHub
3. Create new project
4. Select "Deploy from GitHub repo"
5. Choose your blackbox repo
6. Select the `backend` folder as root directory
7. Add environment variables (if needed)
8. Deploy!

Railway will automatically:
- Detect the Procfile
- Install dependencies from requirements.txt
- Start the app with: uvicorn app:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port $PORT

Your backend URL will be: https://your-app-name.railway.app

## Step 3: Deploy Frontend on Vercel
1. Go to https://vercel.com
2. Sign up with GitHub
3. Import your GitHub repo
4. Configure project:
   - Root Directory: `web`
5. Add Environment Variable:
   - Key: VITE_BACKEND_URL
   - Value: https://your-railway-app-name.railway.app
6. Deploy!

Your frontend will be at: https://your-app-name.vercel.app

## Step 4: Update Backend API Calls
The React app will automatically use the Railway backend URL from the environment variable.
